{"task":{"id":"Prob133_2014_q3fsm","spec":"
I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input  clk
 - input  reset
 - input  s
 - input  w
 - output z

The module should implement a finite state machine with inputs s and w.
Assume that the FSM begins in a reset state called A, as depicted below.
The FSM remains in state A as long as s = 0, and it moves to state B when
s = 1. Once in state B the FSM examines the value of the input w in the
next three clock cycles. If w = 1 in exactly two of these clock cycles,
then the FSM has to set an output z to 1 in the following clock cycle.
Otherwise z has to be 0. The FSM continues checking w for the next three
clock cycles, and so on. Use as few states as possible. Note that the s
input is used only in state A, so you need to consider just the w input.
Assume reset is active high synchronous. Assume all sequential logic is
triggered on the positive edge of the clock.

","interface":{"top":"TopModule","ports":[{"name":"clk","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"reset","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"s","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"w","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"z","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false}]},"constraints":"SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."},"current":{"revision_id":"fb4b4931-dfcd-4e56-b87b-9aa93d386a05","source_sha256":"eee1c2fdb43f0ece5e1db6288c2054018579c91349f7f7207ff6cb0b724f94f1","source":"
module TopModule (
    input clk,
    input reset,
    input s,
    input w,
    output z
);

    localparam A = 3'd0,
               B = 3'd1,
               C = 3'd2,
               D = 3'd3,
               E = 3'd4;

    reg [2:0] state, next_state;
    reg [1:0] cnt;

    always @(*) begin
        case (state)
            A: next_state = s ? B : A;
            B: next_state = C;
            C: next_state = D;
            D: next_state = E;
            E: next_state = B;
            default: next_state = A;
        endcase
    end

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset) begin
            state <= A;
            cnt <= 2'd0;
        end else begin
            state <= next_state;

            if (state == B)
                cnt <= {1'b0, w};
            else if (state == C || state == D)
                cnt <= cnt + {1'b0, w};
            else
                cnt <= 2'd0;
        end
    end

    assign z = (state == E) && (cnt == 2'd2);

endmodule
